{'Name': 'ema_self_distillation', 'Title': 'Online EMA Self-Distillation for Stabilizing Small Character Language Models', 'Experiment': 'Maintain an exponential-moving-average copy of the GPT model during training. After model initialization, create ema_model as a deepcopy of the uncompiled model, freeze its parameters, and update it after each optimizer step with ema_param = decay * ema_param + (1 - decay) * param. In the training loop, compute the normal next-character cross-entropy loss with the student model. In parallel, run ema_model on the same batch under torch.no_grad(), then add a temperature-scaled KL divergence between student logits and EMA-teacher logits: total_loss = ce_loss + alpha * T^2 * KL(log_softmax(student/T), softmax(teacher/T)). Keep generation and validation metrics based on the standard lm_head and next-character loss for comparability. Report best validation loss, convergence speed, total training time, inference speed, and generated samples across shakespeare_char, enwik8, and text8. Run a main setting with ema_decay=0.999, temperature=2.0, alpha=0.2, plus small ablations over alpha in {0.05, 0.1, 0.2}.', 'Interestingness': 7, 'Feasibility': 7, 'Novelty': 5}
Iteration 2/3
