{'Name': 'scheduled_self_conditioning', 'Title': 'Scheduled Self-Conditioning to Reduce Exposure Bias in Character Language Models', 'Experiment': 'Add a training-only scheduled self-conditioning objective. After warmup_iters, run a no-gradient clean forward pass on X to obtain next-token logits. Convert these logits to model-generated candidate tokens using either multinomial sampling at temperature 1.0 or argmax as an ablation. Construct X_self by copying X and replacing a ramped fraction of positions X[:, 1:] with the model predictions from the previous positions, while keeping the original Y targets unchanged. Then run the normal training forward/backward pass on X_self, Y using standard cross-entropy. Ramp replacement_prob linearly from 0 to values such as 0.05 and 0.10 over 1000 iterations after warmup to avoid early instability. Keep estimate_loss, clean validation, checkpointing, and generation unchanged for direct comparison. Add an optional robustness evaluation that applies the same self-conditioning procedure on validation inputs without gradient and reports loss on the original targets. Compare against baseline and random-token corruption using best clean validation loss, self-conditioned validation loss, convergence speed, total train time, inference tokens per second, and generated samples across shakespeare_char, enwik8, and text8.', 'Interestingness': 8, 'Feasibility': 8, 'Novelty': 6}
Iteration 2/3
{'Name': 'self_recovery_training', 'Title': 'Self-Recovery Training for Exposure-Bias-Robust Character Language Models', 'Experiment': 'Add a training-only self-recovery auxiliary objective. In the training loop, compute the standard clean forward pass on X,Y and keep its cross-entropy as the primary loss. After warmup_iters, use the clean logits under torch.no_grad() to produce one-step model predictions for each position, using multinomial sampling at temperature 1.0 as the main setting and argmax as an ablation. Construct X_self by copying X and replacing a small ramped fraction of X[:, 1:] with predictions from logits[:, :-1], so the model conditions on its own plausible previous-token mistakes while targets Y remain unchanged. Run a second forward pass on X_self,Y and train with total_loss = clean_loss + alpha_t * self_loss, where alpha_t ramps from 0 to alpha over 1000 iterations after warmup. Test alpha values such as 0.1 and 0.25 with max replacement probabilities 0.05 and 0.10. Keep normal estimate_loss, clean validation, generation, and final reporting unchanged for comparability. Add a self-conditioned validation probe that applies the same replacement procedure without gradients and reports recovery loss. Compare best clean validation loss, self-conditioned validation loss, convergence speed, total train time, inference tokens per second, and generated samples across shakespeare_char, enwik8, and text8.', 'Interestingness': 8, 'Feasibility': 8, 'Novelty': 6}
