{'Name': 'discounted_future_distribution', 'Title': 'Distance-Discounted Future Distribution Prediction for Autoregressive Representation Learning', 'Experiment': 'Add a lightweight auxiliary objective that asks each hidden state to predict a distance-weighted distribution of characters appearing in its near future. In GPT.__init__, add an optional future_window_head = nn.Linear(n_embd, vocab_size, bias=False). In GPT.forward, keep the standard tied lm_head and next-character cross-entropy unchanged, but when targets are provided and the auxiliary option is enabled, also compute aux_logits = future_window_head(x). For each position, build a soft target distribution from targets[:, t:t+W] using weights gamma^k for future offsets k, normalizing over valid positions; use W=16 and gamma=0.9 as the main setting. Compute auxiliary loss as soft cross-entropy between log_softmax(aux_logits) and this discounted future distribution. Train with total_loss = next_loss + alpha * future_distribution_loss, using alpha=0.1 as the main setting and small ablations alpha=0.05, W in {8, 32}, plus a flat unweighted-window variant. Keep estimate_loss, validation, final reporting, and generation based on the ordinary next-character lm_head for comparability. Compare against the baseline across shakespeare_char, enwik8, and text8 using best validation loss, convergence speed, total training time, inference tokens per second, generated samples, and auxiliary-head parameter overhead.', 'Interestingness': 8, 'Feasibility': 9, 'Novelty': 6}

