{'Name': 'confidence_ngram_distillation', 'Title': 'Confidence-Gated N-Gram Distillation for Sample-Efficient Character Transformers', 'Experiment': "Build a fixed smoothed backoff n-gram teacher from each dataset's train.bin before training, using orders up to 5 and no validation data. Store next-character count dictionaries for each context order and compute a teacher confidence from the selected context count. During training, keep the standard next-character cross-entropy unchanged. After warmup_iters, sample a small subset of token positions from each batch, query the highest-order available teacher distribution for each context, keep and renormalize the top-k teacher probabilities, and add a KL distillation loss between the student's restricted top-k distribution and the teacher's top-k distribution. Weight each sampled position by a confidence factor such as count / (count + c), and ramp the global distillation weight alpha_t from 0 to alpha over 1000 iterations. Validation, generation, and final reporting remain based on ordinary next-character cross-entropy with no n-gram teacher at inference. Compare the baseline against max_order=3 and max_order=5 teachers with top_k=16 and alpha values 0.05 and 0.1 across shakespeare_char, enwik8, and text8. Report best validation loss, early convergence speed, train-time overhead, inference tokens per second, generated samples, teacher coverage, teacher-only validation loss, and student-teacher agreement over training.", 'Interestingness': 8, 'Feasibility': 9, 'Novelty': 6}

