{'Name': 'learned_context_pruning', 'Title': 'Learned Context Pruning for Compression-Robust Autoregressive Transformers', 'Experiment': 'Add a training-time learned context-pruning consistency objective. Extend GPTConfig with use_context_pruning, context_prune_weight, context_keep_ratio, context_prune_ramp_iters, and context_prune_temperature. Modify GPT.forward to optionally accept input_embeds_override and return final logits as usual. In GPT.__init__, add a lightweight salience head nn.Linear(n_embd, 1) that scores token embeddings or early hidden states. During training, first run the clean forward pass on X,Y and compute ordinary next-character cross-entropy. After warmup_iters, use the salience head on detached clean token embeddings or detached early hidden states to select a per-example top-k subset of context positions according to context_keep_ratio, always preserving the current token and the most recent few tokens. Construct a compressed input embedding tensor where unselected history positions are replaced by a learned null-context embedding, then run a second forward pass on the same targets. Add a temperature-scaled KL consistency loss from detached clean logits to pruned-context logits, ramping its weight linearly to context_prune_weight. Keep estimate_loss, validation, generation, and final reporting based on the ordinary clean model for comparability. Add diagnostics that evaluate validation loss under random pruning versus learned pruning at keep ratios such as 0.25, 0.5, and 0.75, plus average selected-token distance and salience entropy. Compare the baseline against learned context pruning with context_keep_ratio=0.5, context_prune_weight values 0.05 and 0.1, and a random-pruning consistency ablation across shakespeare_char, enwik8, and text8.', 'Interestingness': 8, 'Feasibility': 8, 'Novelty': 6}
