{'Name': 'self_contrastive_rollout_ranking', 'Title': 'Self-Contrastive Rollout Ranking for Sequence-Level Autoregressive Training', 'Experiment': 'Keep the standard GPT architecture, generation code, and next-character cross-entropy objective unchanged. Add a helper that scores a prefix-plus-continuation sequence by summing log probabilities only over continuation tokens. In the training loop, after warmup_iters and every rank_interval iterations, take a small sub-batch, choose a real prefix of length prefix_len and its true following continuation of length rollout_len from X, then generate a negative continuation of the same length from the current model under torch.no_grad(). Run gradient-tracked scoring passes on the real and generated continuations conditioned on the same prefix, and add a logistic ranking loss such as -log sigmoid((logp_real - logp_generated) / rank_temperature). Train with total_loss = ce_loss + alpha_t * rank_loss, ramping alpha_t after warmup. Keep estimate_loss, best validation loss, final reporting, and inference speed based on ordinary next-character loss for comparability. Add diagnostics for rollout ranking accuracy, average real-vs-generated log probability gap, repeated n-gram rates, generated entropy, and training-time overhead. Compare the baseline against alpha values such as 0.03, 0.05, and 0.1, with prefix_len=128, rollout_len=32, and rank_interval values such as 5 or 10 across shakespeare_char, enwik8, and text8.', 'Interestingness': 8, 'Feasibility': 8, 'Novelty': 7}
