{'Name': 'causal_virtual_adversarial_training', 'Title': 'Causal Virtual Adversarial Training for Locally Smooth Autoregressive Language Models', 'Experiment': 'Modify GPT.forward to optionally accept input_embeds_override and optionally return clean token embeddings before position embeddings. In the training loop, keep the standard clean forward pass on X,Y and optimize ordinary next-character cross-entropy as the primary loss. After warmup_iters, compute detached clean predictive distributions from the clean logits. Build a small random perturbation tensor on the token embeddings, normalize it by embedding RMS, enable gradients on it, and run one adversarial probe forward pass through the same model using input_embeds_override=clean_embeds + perturbation. Compute KL divergence from detached clean probabilities to probe logits, backpropagate only to the perturbation, normalize the resulting perturbation gradient to obtain the virtual adversarial direction, then run a second forward pass with clean_embeds + vat_epsilon * adversarial_direction. Add a temperature-scaled KL consistency loss between detached clean logits and adversarial logits, ramping its weight alpha_t from 0 to alpha after warmup. Keep estimate_loss, best validation loss, generation, final reporting, and inference speed based on the ordinary clean model. Add diagnostics for validation loss under random embedding noise, validation loss under one-step adversarial embedding perturbations, predictive KL sharpness, calibration by confidence bucket, and train-time overhead. Compare the baseline against vat_epsilon values such as 0.5, 1.0, and 2.0 times normalized embedding RMS with alpha values 0.03 and 0.1 across shakespeare_char, enwik8, and text8.', 'Interestingness': 8, 'Feasibility': 8, 'Novelty': 6}
