Sample 1:
 the conveyance of the Duke of York.

YORK:
Farewell, my lord. Then for I will show thee
I protest thee from the ungrateful hollow:
For what have I in her, there part the grace
And sleep into her face against the gates,
And without conduct herself a man to fear.

GLOUCESTER:
The matter; blows the wisest prince, that doth the
complaint of the earth and the chasing with the coronation
with her tenderness of the princess that doth grant him soundly.
What thinkest thou, England's royal king be right,
